Title: MIDNIGHT IN KOWLOON: DAYS OF RAIN
Genre: Romance / Impressionist Cinema
Recommended Style: Wong Kar-wai Impressionist

EXT. KOWLOON NOODLE STALL - NIGHT - RAIN
[STYLE: Wong Kar-wai Impressionist | LIGHTING: Saturated Neon Amber, Step-Printed Motion Blur]

Steam from a boiling noodle cauldron mingles with tropical downpour. Red and gold neon signs blur into shimmering pools of memory.

MR. CHOW (40s, tailored 1960s suit, umbrella held low) pauses at the corner of the narrow alleyway.

MRS. CHAN (30s, high-collared cheongsam with floral silk embroidery, holding a thermos container) walks slowly past him in the rain.

Their shoulders graze for a fleeting second. Neither speaks, but their eyes meet through the descending water droplets.

MR. CHOW
(softly, into the rain)
If there was an extra ticket... would you come with me?

Mrs. Chan pauses at the stairs. A tear mixes with rain on her cheek.
